Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||08-03-2001||10:31 AM||||If I did the math right thats 244,000 miles on the car.<P> if the engine is not rebuilt, and the tranny, CVs, suspension everything... then you are in for major work.<P> my rule of thumb for a well designed and maintained car is to expect 160 to 200k MILES out of it on the first go around - TOPS!<P> then if you replace/rebuild engine, tranny, suspension parts, you can expect maybe half that again with the new stuff - TOPS<P> go over those records carefully - anything that hasnt been rebuilt or replaced  recently is gonna be your project - IE if the engine was replaced at 200 km then its probally due again.||||reg||1
